# Trak — MVP Requirements (first pilot)

Status: proposed by Imad, 23 September 2026. Becomes the agreed pilot scope
when it merges to main with a non-author approval (docs/release/merge-gate.md).
Replaces the April 2026 "pilot wedge" requirements (REQ-001 to REQ-005 and
the 60% player-logging hypothesis). Those, and the April PRD, architecture,
roadmap and milestone plans, are in git history at commit 9114f4c.

Progress against this scope is tracked in docs/use-cases/PILOT-INDEX.md.


## The idea

Build a few essential journeys to a high standard and ship them sooner. Every
other feature shows "coming soon". A PR that serves none of the journeys or
guarantees below waits until the pilot has started.

The loop:

  Academy registers the child -> parent consents -> child activates their
  account -> coach logs the match or training -> coach assesses and writes a
  message -> the player sees the message; the parent sees the bands.

Cohort: one whole squad at one UAE academy, chosen by the academy, for eight
weeks. The academy and the player count are not agreed yet. Rehearse for 25.


## P0 journeys (the non-negotiables)

J1. Academy admission (concierge)
  - The academy gives Trak its roster: child name, date of birth, age group,
    assigned coach, child email and every guardian email. Trak loads it by
    hand. The academy console shows "coming soon".
  - Only rostered children get in. The backend refuses player and parent
    profiles that have no valid invitation. Hiding the signup screen is not
    enough.
  - Children do not join by typing a name or a coach code, and coaches do not
    add players.
  - A player cannot change their own date of birth. A missing date of birth
    counts as a minor.

J2. Parent consent
  - The invitation goes to the guardian emails the academy supplied, is sent
    when the child is admitted, and arrives in under 60 seconds at Gmail and
    Outlook, not in spam. It names the child, the academy and the purpose, and
    carries Trak branding and a safe-sender line.
  - One required consent covers coach records, assessments, the published
    message, and viewing by the child and their linked parents. It is stored
    with the guardian's name, relationship and the notice version. The screen
    promises nothing the system does not enforce.
  - Each guardian has their own sign-in, linked to the child. One guardian
    can consent for siblings without a second account.
  - Withdrawal is one tap from the parent profile while signed in. It takes
    effect immediately, including for sessions that are already open.

J3. Child activation
  - Only after consent, the child gets a one-use invitation at the email the
    academy supplied. First send, resend, expiry, wrong account and existing
    account all behave safely.
  - A forgotten password uses the standard reset to the child's email. If an
    address is wrong, Trak corrects it by hand and records who changed it and
    when.

J4. Coach logs
  - Match: date, opponent, result, and each child's position, minutes, goals
    and assists, with no invented defaults. This uses the existing `matches`
    table and `log_match_for_player`, which still needs a consent check.
  - Training: date, type and session notes, using the existing
    `coach_sessions` table.
  - Every write checks consent and the coach's academy assignment. A retry
    never creates a duplicate and never silently loses data.

J5. Coach assessment and message
  - The coach's squad marks each player "Ready to assess" or "Waiting for
    parent". A waiting player cannot be opened, and the reason is shown in
    plain words. If consent is withdrawn while the form is open, the save
    fails with a plain message and the values the coach entered are kept.
  - Everything is on one screen: six sliders produce the band, then two boxes.
    "Message to [first name]: only [first name] sees this." and an
    optional "Private note: only you can see this."
  - Parents never see the coach's message; they see the bands. Decided by
    Imad on 25 September 2026 after the second use-case test: a message
    parents also read doubles the coach's workload and invites parent-coach
    friction. Revisit with pilot feedback (TRAK-63).
  - One Save button: saving sends the message to the player; nothing reaches
    them before the coach saves (Imad, 25 September 2026, TRAK-64). If only
    part of a save works, the screen says what was saved and what was not.
  - An assessment belongs to a session that already happened: the session is
    required and there is one assessment per player per session (Imad, 25
    September 2026, TRAK-68).
  - Quick Assess is hidden for the pilot. /coach/assess is the only
    assessment screen (see "Coming soon" below).

J6. Player and parent see it
  - Player home shows the latest band, the six bars and the coach's message,
    marked "new" until opened. Before the first assessment it says the player
    is waiting for their coach, not "Your card is ready".
  - Player and parent see the match and training history the coach logged.
  - A parent sees the same bands and history for the selected child, but
    not the coach's message (J5). With siblings, it shows the right child
    every time.
  - A failed load shows a clear error and a retry button. It never shows an
    empty state that looks like "no data" (UC-X02).

J7. Measure
  - On any pilot day, answer in under a minute: assessments per coach this
    week, and player and parent opens this week. Count real UI events only,
    not seeded or synthetic accounts.
  - Opening a published message is recorded as a UI event.


## Guarantees

The database enforces these, not the UI. Each is proven by a negative test
run under a real authenticated role.

G1. No development record exists about an under-18 without active consent, on
    every write path: assessments, awards, `log_match_for_player`, shared
    feedback.
G2. A child cannot approve themselves, change their age or choose their
    guardian's email.
G3. No child sees another child's data, and no academy sees another
    academy's data.
G4. Nothing reaches a child that a coach did not write and publish. Private
    notes stay private.
G5. No message about a child goes to the wrong adult.
G6. Withdrawal stops processing and hides published content immediately.
G7. No AI processing, passport or export, and no child photos, in either the
    UI or the backend.

Bypass attempts that must fail against the API: self-signup without an
invitation, changing a date of birth, linking by name or code, a coach
writing for a waiting player, reading private notes, and reading another
child's records.


## Success

Quality bar: no P0 journey fails during the eight weeks. A manual workaround
keeps other work moving, but it does not count as a pass. The journey must be
repaired and retested.

Value (proposed; founders set the targets before launch):
  - Share of published coach messages that the player opens
    within 7 days.
  - Share of players who receive at least one published message every 14
    days.


## Coming soon (by route, from src/App.tsx)

"Coming soon" means the route shows a static placeholder AND its backend
writes are closed. Hiding a button is not enough.

P0, must work:
  /, /auth/confirm, /reset-password, /onboarding/:role (invitation only),
  /parent-invite, /parent-info, /parent/home, /parent/matches,
  /parent/consent, /parent/profile, /coach/home, /coach/squad,
  /coach/player/:id, /coach/assess, /coach/sessions, /coach/sessions/add,
  /coach/sessions/quick, /coach/sessions/list, /coach/profile,
  /coach/manual, /player/home, /player/feedback/:assessmentId,
  /player/matches, /player/match/:id, /player/profile, /profile,
  /settings, /dashboard

  /coach/sessions/quick stays: it is the "Match" entry from
  /coach/sessions and opens the same screen as /coach/sessions/add in
  match mode. It is J4's match-logging path.

Coming soon:
  /player/passport, /player/evolution, /coach/feedback/:assessmentId (AI
  draft review), /coach/assistant, /coach/schedule, /coach/recognition,
  /coach/award, /parent/alerts, /club/home, /club/squads, /club/coaches,
  /club/profile, /club/radar

  The academy console is coming soon because the concierge roster (J1)
  replaces it. /club/home is also where an academy director lands after
  sign-in, so the placeholder must render there without errors.

Remove for the pilot:
  /coach/squad/add (the academy registers players). Remove avatar upload
  from every profile page.
  /coach/quick-assess: hidden. It saves sliders and a private note but has
  no message to the player and no publish step, so it cannot meet J5. A
  second assessment screen would also need its own proof for G1 and G4.
  Its two entry points (the Coach Home button and the post-match prompt)
  go to /coach/assess instead.

Route calls decided by Kostas on 23 September 2026 (TRAK-43).


## Cut from the pilot

  - AI feedback, the assistant and schedule parsing. Child data would go to a
    third party without processor paperwork.
  - Passport, export and sharing.
  - Child photos and avatars, until storage access and backup are fixed.
  - Recognition and awards.
  - Parent goals.
  - Player-entered match logging (UC-A02/A03 are parked).
  - Lead guardian inviting another adult. The academy supplies every guardian.
  - A separate "household" entity. Guardians who each link to the child
    already get the same result.
  - Per-child training notes. The published message is the child-specific
    text.
  - Transfers between academies. One academy, one squad: founders handle any
    change by hand.
  - Automatic retry. A clear error with a retry button is enough.


## First after the pilot starts

Events: the coach schedules training and matches, the family sees a calendar
with Google and Apple sync, and the coach marks attendance. RSVP is not
agreed. Then the home screen for each role (design work in the pilot-demo
channels). Other coming-soon items have no agreed order.


## Launch gate for real children

Real children join only when all of these pass and a majority of founders
says go. A date on its own never admits anyone.

  1. Every P0 journey passes on the deployed build, on two real phones,
     with synthetic identities and approved inboxes. Use three children: two
     siblings, and one whose guardian withholds consent. Then withdraw
     consent for one child.
  2. Every guarantee's negative test passes against the deployed backend.
  3. A synthetic 25-player squad runs with no errors.
  4. A signed academy pilot agreement, and terms accepted.
  5. Counsel signs off on data roles, the notice, withdrawal and deletion,
     and retention. The proposed retention is the pilot plus 90 days.
  6. A backup and a written recovery runbook exist. The restore has not been
     rehearsed, and the go decision records that risk.
  7. A named support inbox. The founders jointly own support and escalation.
  8. `pilot_config` points at the real academy. Today it points at
     "Rehearsal FC", starting 28 September.

Friday 25 September is a synthetic demo, not admission.

Incidents: for a wrong recipient, a consent bypass or a cross-child read,
pause the affected scope and new admissions at once. A founder majority
decides the restart, subject to legal duties.


